WEBVTT

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:12.080
"I'm not about to lose my head for anything,"

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:13.830
was the thought that sealed my fate!

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:15.500
Hey, you're being too self-centered, Appare!

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.200
I got dragged along with the departing Appare,

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.370
and before I knew it, it was the Pacific Ocean!

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:22.790
We got taken aboard by another ship
and rescued, but this is America!

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:24.950
Los Angeles?!

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:09.200
"Episode 2"
"In the Dark"

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:20.120
Wow, this is something else.

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:23.000
Good. No problem with the engine.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:28.500
Can you repair the ship, Appare?!
When will we be able to get back to Japan?!

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:29.370
Not a chance.

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:30.620
Huh? Why not?

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:31.950
I'm not repairing the ship.

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:32.830
Why not?!

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:34.410
Because it's an experimental ship.

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:35.790
So what if it is?!

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:37.120
You ask a lot of questions.

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:40.660
You don't explain a lot! Help me to understand!

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:42.580
I've accomplished the point of the experiment,

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:44.870
so fixing it up the way it was
would be pointless.

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:49.000
Besides, it's impossible to cross
the Pacific with the range this ship has.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.250
Then you could always improve it, couldn't you?

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:54.200
There are any number of
rudimentary steamships around

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:55.700
good enough to cross the Pacific.

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:58.620
When you say "rudimentary,"
are you talking about our ship?

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:00.330
--That's right.
--He is not!

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:03.950
Hey, don't be so rude!
It's thanks to the captain here

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.580
that we're being allowed to
stay here for a little while!

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:09.290
Don't worry about it.

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:11.410
We haven't used this storehouse in a while.

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:14.000
You're free to use it until someone
comes along wanting to rent it.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.370
In return,

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:18.040
you don't mind if I keep this, do you?

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:19.290
Suit yourself.

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:23.500
While you're at it, I don't suppose you'd be
open to taking us back to Japan...?

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:26.950
Don't be an idiot. You think I'm
going to take you out to sea for free?

00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:31.040
Ordinarily, I'd want the fare
for your passage as it is.

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:32.500
Isn't there anything I can do?!

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:35.250
I can clean, or cook, or do whatever you like!

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:37.700
I already have professional cooks and cleaners.

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:40.910
He might be one thing, but what else can you do?

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:41.750
Huh?

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:45.000
Besides, it's not like I can hire
a crewman who's gonna jump ship

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:47.790
when we get to his destination.

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:49.160
In any case,

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:52.040
we're about to head through
the Panama Canal to the Atlantic.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:54.450
We won't be going to Japan for a while.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:56.160
I see...

00:03:56.160 --> 00:04:00.080
First thing you should do is find a job.
If you don't work, you shan't eat.

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:02.080
And if you work like mad for ten years,

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:05.370
you might be able to charter
a ship back to your own country.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:14.040
This is the other side of the ocean...

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:18.250
The country that made the steamships.

00:04:20.290 --> 00:04:22.700
Can't you see your way somehow?
I'll do anything!

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:24.450
We're a service industry.

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:27.620
We can't very well hire someone
from only God knows where!

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:29.700
What do you mean, only God knows where?

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:33.000
I was born and raised in Shibaura, Fuyutsuki!

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:35.500
My family name is Isshiki,
and my given name is Kosame--

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:37.450
There are steam-powered cars all over the place.

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:39.700
--Damn it! Appare, you should work, too!
--I'd sure like to take one apart.

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:42.040
--Damn it! Appare, you should work, too!
--I just have to put it together again, right?

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:43.160
Huh?

00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:45.830
Hire you?

00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:47.040
Yeah.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:50.450
I just have a small shop. I have enough help.

00:04:50.450 --> 00:04:52.000
Then that's perfect.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:56.000
It's not like I want to work anyway.
I welcome the free time.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:58.700
As long as you pay me a wage,
there's no problem.

00:05:00.830 --> 00:05:01.870
Huh?

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:06.830
How did you do? Find anything?

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:11.450
No. They aren't hiring where I want to work,

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:14.120
and I don't want to work where they are hiring.

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:18.580
Huh? What do you mean? You have to look harder.

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:21.830
There are three things you need in life--

00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:24.120
your pride, what you're eating now,

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:26.580
and the money to buy
what you're eating tomorrow.

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:28.700
This is not the Japan we're familiar with.

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:31.250
No matter what we have in reserve,
we can't rest easy.

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:34.040
--Never mind that we're penniless--
--How about that?

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:47.500
--Let him have it!
--Hey switch with me! I'll get him!

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:49.620
All right, I'm gonna lay him out!

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:04.620
Isn't that enough, Appare?
I didn't study swordsmanship for <i>this</i>--

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:06.290
I'm next.

00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:10.750
That's three minutes' worth. One round.

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:13.830
I don't need the stick.

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:16.950
I was a pro boxer back in the day.

00:06:16.950 --> 00:06:22.790
I see, a pugilist. I will reciprocate
your pride with my own.

00:06:22.790 --> 00:06:25.620
I don't care. You can hit me back.

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:28.080
If you want to stay alive, that is!

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:47.330
Do you wish to continue?

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:52.700
You're better than I thought, Kosame.

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:56.200
Well, you know... I read my
opponent's intent and move first.

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:59.080
All of the skills in the Hangetsu
Ittoryu School derive from--

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:00.750
You have to get hit once in a while,

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:03.200
or people are going to stop paying, you know.

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:04.790
Then <i>you </i>do it.

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:06.950
No. That would hurt.

00:07:08.540 --> 00:07:12.620
Well, we should get something to eat now.
All that exercise made me hungry.

00:07:24.450 --> 00:07:26.450
What kind of car is that?

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:37.870
Ah, hey! Appare!

00:07:46.330 --> 00:07:49.040
It looks like it takes money to get inside.

00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:54.330
Ah, hey! We need that for--

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:06.660
What is this?

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:11.870
Oh, I get it.

00:08:11.870 --> 00:08:15.870
They're racing to see which car is fastest.

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:20.200
Amazing. The cars are the stars here.

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:21.580
Welcome...

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:26.620
...to today's unveiling of the car
that's the pride of Great Motors!

00:08:26.620 --> 00:08:28.910
The engine is 7200ccs,

00:08:28.910 --> 00:08:31.540
with a maximum output of about 200 horsepower!

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:34.450
--Off the record, her top speed is...
--Mr. Dylan, why are you in this race?

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:36.910
If you win the grand prize,
what will you use the money for?

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:39.370
There are stories that you're
competing with Iron Motors,

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:40.580
and looking for Thousand Three...

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:42.620
Allow me to introduce the ultimate driver,

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:45.790
who will be driving our speed machine.

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:47.790
Ask <i>him </i>your questions.

00:08:51.870 --> 00:08:54.200
Hey, Xialian, over here, too!

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:55.700
Oh, okay.

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:59.040
As a member of the Big Three
automotive association, B.I.G.BOSS,

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:02.620
who is sponsoring the Trans-America Wild Race,

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:07.160
I proudly put up this machine!
You are free to compete.

00:09:07.160 --> 00:09:09.330
If you think you have what it takes
to beat this machine,

00:09:09.330 --> 00:09:11.870
you are free to make your challenge at any time!

00:09:11.870 --> 00:09:14.620
There is a total of 1.51
million dollars up for grabs!

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:17.080
Let's cross the American wilderness together,

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:21.120
and mark a new page in history!

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:25.580
--Good grief, to drive at ridiculous
speeds for no good reason,
--And that is the American Dream!

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:28.910
and across the continent, for that matter.
Who does that appeal to...?

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:30.290
I'm going to enter.

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:31.290
Huh?

00:09:32.330 --> 00:09:35.790
I'm going to enter this race.

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:43.700
It would be quickest to revamp
the steam engine and use it,

00:09:43.700 --> 00:09:46.910
but their cars don't run on steam.

00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:50.750
Considering our cruising range
and our total mileage...

00:09:50.750 --> 00:09:51.370
--This is no good. I need
more thorough information.

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:55.250
--I'm sure Father and Fumi are worried.
--This is no good. I need
more thorough information.

00:09:57.870 --> 00:10:01.250
When will I ever be able to get back to Japan?

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:04.330
You want to go home that badly?

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:07.040
Well of course I do! I have a family!

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:11.040
And I can't keep my fiancée
waiting forever, either.

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:14.500
They probably think you're dead,
and your engagement has been broken off.

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:16.000
Huh?!

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:17.120
Feel better now?

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:21.160
Do I <i>look </i>like I feel better?!
"Ah, good, they think I'm dead."

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:25.160
Who thinks like that, really?! Aw, man!

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:27.410
Kosame, you're a complex man.

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:31.620
We can go back to Japan using the prize money.

00:10:32.790 --> 00:10:34.250
Huh?

00:10:34.250 --> 00:10:36.580
If we win, we get a million dollars.

00:10:36.580 --> 00:10:39.370
There's no way we can win.

00:10:39.370 --> 00:10:43.410
If you want to toil away
for ten years, suit yourself.

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:51.120
But I'm doing this. I will cross
this continent faster than anybody.

00:10:53.290 --> 00:10:56.410
If you don't want to, I'll only need
one seat in my car, right?

00:10:56.410 --> 00:11:00.250
Huh? No! N-No...

00:11:00.250 --> 00:11:02.200
No idea, kid.

00:11:02.200 --> 00:11:05.700
Have you seen him?
A man with this tattoo on his neck?

00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:07.120
Get lost.

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:10.910
Hey, don't touch me!

00:11:10.910 --> 00:11:12.660
Ah, hey!

00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:14.000
Are you okay, little boy?

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:17.160
Where are we, at the zoo?

00:11:18.910 --> 00:11:21.250
Ah, little boy...

00:11:21.250 --> 00:11:23.200
I'm not a little boy.

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:24.290
Huh?

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:28.750
You're not him.

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:35.620
What was that?

00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:47.830
Hold on, hold on, hold on! You said
we were just going to look from outside!

00:11:47.830 --> 00:11:51.410
Yeah. Tonight, we're just going to
look at the cars from the outside.

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:53.660
What's the point of looking at them
from outside the building?

00:11:53.660 --> 00:11:56.120
No, but we can't go in there without permission!

00:11:56.120 --> 00:11:58.750
Trespassing is the first step to burglary.

00:11:58.750 --> 00:12:02.120
If we're going to enter the race,
we need to see the real thing for ourselves.

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:04.160
You want to go back to Japan, don't you?

00:12:21.660 --> 00:12:24.950
It's dark in here. We need some kind of light.

00:12:24.950 --> 00:12:27.950
Ah! For the love of...

00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:03.950
In all this darkness? Incredible...

00:13:05.750 --> 00:13:07.200
Ah, Appare!

00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:08.620
Watch yourself!

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:22.120
Are you okay?!

00:13:22.120 --> 00:13:23.290
Yeah.

00:13:31.250 --> 00:13:33.250
Oh, no...

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:38.700
Are you hurt?

00:13:41.370 --> 00:13:42.790
Who are you?!

00:13:42.790 --> 00:13:44.620
Huh? You're a woman?

00:13:44.620 --> 00:13:46.450
What are you doing in here?!

00:13:46.450 --> 00:13:48.250
Oh, uh, well...

00:13:48.250 --> 00:13:50.700
We came to see the cars. Let me have a look.

00:13:50.700 --> 00:13:52.620
--Hey!
--H-Hold on!

00:13:52.620 --> 00:13:55.120
We aren't criminals, or anything...

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:56.330
A katana?!

00:13:57.950 --> 00:13:59.330
Stay away from me!

00:13:59.330 --> 00:14:02.790
It's because of you that my precious car...

00:14:02.790 --> 00:14:05.540
That was quite a kick, for a woman.

00:14:05.540 --> 00:14:08.200
So what if I am a woman?

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:11.200
W-Wait! I don't want to fight you!

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:14.160
Then get rid of your weapon!

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:18.200
This isn't something I can just lay down.

00:14:18.200 --> 00:14:19.700
If you must hit me, then hit me!

00:14:24.040 --> 00:14:25.750
Ah, I knew it!

00:14:27.120 --> 00:14:30.410
Hey, this is a gasoline-powered car, right?

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:35.080
What are you doing, Kosame?

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:44.620
Ow! Ooh...

00:14:45.870 --> 00:14:48.790
--Total displacement is about 6200ccs...

00:14:48.790 --> 00:14:51.410
--So, you really just wanted to see the cars?
--Total displacement is about 6200ccs...

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:52.370
--So, you really just wanted to see the cars?
--Estimated top speed is 95mph.
Is that theoretical?

00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:57.330
--Yeah. My name is Isshiki Kosame.
That's Sorano Appare.
--Estimated top speed is 95mph.
Is that theoretical?

00:14:57.330 --> 00:15:01.910
--I'm sorry we came in uninvited.
I hope we can keep this amicable.
--Propulsion mechanism is a driveshaft.

00:15:01.910 --> 00:15:04.750
--I'm in the same situation,
so I have no room to talk.
--Front and rear independent leaf suspension.

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:05.250
--I'm in the same situation,
so I have no room to talk.
--The rear wheels use a light alloy.

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:06.250
--Huh?
--The rear wheels use a light alloy.

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:07.750
--I'm just a chore girl, but I snuck in
on my own to drive one of the cars.
--The rear wheels use a light alloy.

00:15:07.750 --> 00:15:11.040
--I'm just a chore girl, but I snuck in
on my own to drive one of the cars.
--Not steel discs, but aluminum?

00:15:11.040 --> 00:15:12.790
You're a chore girl?

00:15:12.790 --> 00:15:13.870
Yeah.

00:15:22.160 --> 00:15:27.540
When I was a child, I looked up to
the racers, and joined their team

00:15:27.540 --> 00:15:29.950
as a chore girl.

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:33.620
However, the first thing I learned...

00:15:33.620 --> 00:15:36.160
Girls can't be racers.

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:38.910
Yeah, that's for sure.

00:15:38.910 --> 00:15:42.200
There's no way a woman can drive a car.

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:44.870
The passenger seat is the place for a lady.

00:15:44.870 --> 00:15:46.950
If a woman wants to drive a car,

00:15:46.950 --> 00:15:50.580
she should be in the circus, not on the circuit.

00:15:50.580 --> 00:15:51.830
Listen to me, Jing.

00:15:51.830 --> 00:15:55.200
Racing is a man's profession.
Strength and daring!

00:15:55.200 --> 00:16:01.250
Cars don't run on gasoline;
they run on a man's fiery spirit!

00:16:01.250 --> 00:16:04.660
The world has no female racers.

00:16:05.580 --> 00:16:08.580
Then, the reason you were driving that car...

00:16:08.580 --> 00:16:13.580
Was simply to blow off some steam.
But that's all over now.

00:16:13.580 --> 00:16:17.330
I damaged the car. I'm going to get fired.

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:19.950
No, I'll be worse than fired.

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:23.330
We'll swear we didn't see anything.

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:26.290
I can't lie to the rest of the team.

00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:29.330
Racers put their lives in
the hands of mechanics.

00:16:29.330 --> 00:16:32.370
I can't stay on the team if it means lying.

00:16:32.370 --> 00:16:38.160
Huh? But you're not a racer.
Women don't get to be racers, right?

00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:39.290
Right.

00:16:39.290 --> 00:16:41.120
Then why?

00:16:41.120 --> 00:16:46.790
Even if the world won't allow
a woman to be a racer,

00:16:46.790 --> 00:16:50.700
I don't want to do anything that would
disqualify me from being one.

00:16:52.830 --> 00:16:56.290
I... must sound like a fool.

00:16:56.290 --> 00:16:57.290
Hey!

00:16:58.250 --> 00:17:01.330
How far does this drive on a single tank?

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:04.290
--Huh?
--Hey, now isn't the time.

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:07.790
50, maybe 55 miles, I'd say.

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:09.290
And the tank is 40 liters?

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:11.040
43.

00:17:11.040 --> 00:17:13.330
1.2 miles per liter...

00:17:13.330 --> 00:17:15.290
Why are you asking about that?

00:17:15.290 --> 00:17:18.750
We're building our own car to
enter in the cross-country race.

00:17:18.750 --> 00:17:20.700
Huh? You guys are?

00:17:20.700 --> 00:17:23.160
That's right. And we're gonna win.

00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:28.620
You guys are more dumbasses
who are in it for the money, too, huh?

00:17:28.620 --> 00:17:30.750
Where are you going to get
the money to build it with?

00:17:30.750 --> 00:17:33.330
Do you know how to drive through
the wilderness without any roads?

00:17:33.330 --> 00:17:36.750
Can you defend yourselves from
outlaws in dangerous areas?

00:17:36.750 --> 00:17:39.580
If you're lucky, you'll drop out
before you leave Los Angeles,

00:17:39.580 --> 00:17:42.410
and if you're not, you'll die
broken down in the wilderness.

00:17:42.410 --> 00:17:44.330
Die in the wilderness?

00:17:44.330 --> 00:17:46.620
It wouldn't be any fun if it were easy.

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:47.500
Huh?

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:50.160
Doing something that nobody else could do...

00:17:50.160 --> 00:17:52.660
Someday, I'm gonna stun the world.

00:17:53.870 --> 00:17:56.620
Nobody else can do it because it's impossible!

00:17:56.620 --> 00:18:01.500
What's impossible and what is thought of
as impossible are two different things.

00:18:01.500 --> 00:18:05.370
Is it impossible for a woman to be a racer?

00:18:05.370 --> 00:18:10.620
How come? Your driving is as good
as those guys were this afternoon.

00:18:10.620 --> 00:18:12.580
You also know a lot about cars.

00:18:12.580 --> 00:18:14.660
What do you even know?!

00:18:14.660 --> 00:18:16.620
I don't know; that's why I'm asking.

00:18:16.620 --> 00:18:20.870
Why do you let others decide
how far you're able to go?

00:18:25.040 --> 00:18:27.290
Stop it, Appare.

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:29.000
There are things in the world

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:34.000
that people like you who have
nothing to lose wouldn't understand.

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:35.750
Oh, yeah?

00:18:35.750 --> 00:18:37.790
You're a complex girl, huh?

00:18:40.250 --> 00:18:45.290
Either way, it's too late.
I'm going to get fired tomorrow.

00:18:48.370 --> 00:18:51.790
See you. You broke in here without asking,

00:18:51.790 --> 00:18:53.410
so make sure you lock up when you leave.

00:18:53.410 --> 00:18:55.870
Huh? Oh, hey...

00:18:55.870 --> 00:18:58.750
What's your name?

00:18:58.750 --> 00:19:02.370
Xialian. Jing Xialian.

00:19:02.370 --> 00:19:05.410
You have my gratitude, Miss Xialian.

00:19:05.410 --> 00:19:10.580
Look around all you like. There's no way
you'll be able to build a car anyway.

00:19:38.620 --> 00:19:40.540
Here you go. Today's clothes.

00:19:40.540 --> 00:19:42.120
Thanks.

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:44.750
Mom?

00:19:45.790 --> 00:19:48.080
Would you be happy if I took over the business?

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:52.410
Well, sure I would. We're always
so busy, and shorthanded.

00:19:52.410 --> 00:19:55.370
You're our only child. Someday,
you have to get married,

00:19:55.370 --> 00:19:57.660
and inherit the business from us.

00:19:57.660 --> 00:20:02.040
Okay. Well, I'm off.

00:20:02.040 --> 00:20:04.950
What? You broke Number 4?

00:20:04.950 --> 00:20:08.040
Yes. Last night, I was driving it
without permission--

00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:09.410
What are you talking about?

00:20:09.410 --> 00:20:11.870
Did you dream it or something? See for yourself.

00:20:11.870 --> 00:20:14.250
Number 4 is in top form.

00:20:14.250 --> 00:20:15.250
Huh?

00:20:21.120 --> 00:20:22.120
How...?

00:20:22.120 --> 00:20:25.040
It's just a test run,
and it set a new course record.

00:20:25.040 --> 00:20:25.620
--Hey, get Number 3 on the course already!

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:27.950
--I-It couldn't be... <i>them</i>?
--Hey, get Number 3 on the course already!

00:20:27.950 --> 00:20:30.040
Hey, Jing, you too.

00:20:30.040 --> 00:20:32.000
Don't just stand there, get to work.

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:33.620
Oh, right.

00:20:35.700 --> 00:20:37.580
You're amazing, you know.

00:20:37.580 --> 00:20:41.870
The engine was fine,
and they had more than enough parts.

00:20:43.040 --> 00:20:46.330
Even if the world won't allow it, huh?

00:20:47.200 --> 00:20:50.790
I think I kind of know what that's like.

00:20:50.790 --> 00:20:54.540
They tell me the world is changing,
and I should give up my katana,

00:20:54.540 --> 00:21:00.120
but that's not so easy to do.
Even if I can't draw it now...

00:21:05.370 --> 00:21:08.040
Okay, let's head back and eat supper.

00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:15.120
It's lucky for us that storehouse
has living quarters, huh?

00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:18.080
Like they say, good feeding
before good breeding--

00:21:21.250 --> 00:21:23.620
What was that about a tattoo?

00:21:25.790 --> 00:21:28.830
What are you planning to do with that?

00:21:31.910 --> 00:21:34.540
H-Hey! That's enough, already!

00:21:34.540 --> 00:21:36.330
A bunch of grown men against one child?

00:21:36.330 --> 00:21:39.040
Who are you? This kid's old man?

00:21:39.040 --> 00:21:40.200
Actually, no, I'm--

00:21:40.200 --> 00:21:41.580
Then shut up!

00:21:41.580 --> 00:21:45.830
We have to teach the barbarians
the rules of this country.

00:21:47.450 --> 00:21:49.000
A gun?!

00:22:00.660 --> 00:22:02.080
Kosame?

00:22:02.080 --> 00:22:04.000
He's freaked out.

00:22:10.200 --> 00:22:12.000
Wh-Who are you?!

00:22:14.620 --> 00:22:17.290
Keep it down.

00:22:17.290 --> 00:22:19.290
You're ruining my buzz.

00:23:46.700 --> 00:23:47.330
"Next time"

00:23:47.330 --> 00:23:49.910
"Episode 3"
"Duel"
